{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"# Week 8 Capstone — Meeting-to-Action Assistant\n\nSelf-contained COSC 650 capstone. Reuses **Week 3 structured output**, **Week 4 validation**, **Week 5 MiniLM+FAISS RAG**, **Week 6 cross-encoder reranking**, and **Week 7 dynamic few-shot selection**.\n\nArchitecture: transcript → retrieval → reranking → optional examples → Gemini Flash → validation → metrics/judge/failure trace. A small local Qwen model is measured separately for narrow classification."},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"# Uncomment once in a fresh Colab runtime:\n# %pip install -q sentence-transformers faiss-cpu openai pandas numpy tabulate transformers torch\nimport os,re,json,time,math,hashlib,random\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd,faiss\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer,CrossEncoder\nfrom IPython.display import display,Markdown\ntry:\n from google.colab import userdata\n if not os.getenv('GEMINI_API_KEY'):\n  k=userdata.get('GEMINI_API_KEY')\n  if k: os.environ['GEMINI_API_KEY']=k\nexcept Exception: pass\nGEMINI_MODEL=os.getenv('GEMINI_MODEL','gemini-3.5-flash')\nJUDGE_MODEL=os.getenv('GEMINI_JUDGE_MODEL',GEMINI_MODEL)\nQWEN_MODEL='Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct'\nMAX_SYNTHESIS_CALLS,MAX_JUDGE_CALLS,MAX_CLASSIFIER_CALLS=30,10,1\nCACHE={'synthesis':{},'judge':{},'classifier':{}}\nLIVE_SYNTHESIS=LIVE_JUDGE=LIVE_CLASSIFIER=0\ndef key(x): return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(x,sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\ndef cli():\n from openai import OpenAI\n return OpenAI(api_key=os.environ['GEMINI_API_KEY'],base_url='https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/')\ndef call(model,msgs,tries=6):\n ds=[2,4,8,16,32]\n for i in range(tries):\n  try:return cli().chat.completions.create(model=model,messages=msgs,temperature=0)\n  except Exception as e:\n   s=getattr(e,'status_code',None)\n   if s not in {429,500,502,503,504} or i==tries-1: raise\n   w=ds[min(i,4)]+random.random(); print(f'Gemini {s}; retry {w:.1f}s'); time.sleep(w)\ndef pj(s): return json.loads(re.sub(r'^```(?:json)?\\s*|\\s*```$','',s.strip(),flags=re.I))\nprint('Gemini:',GEMINI_MODEL,'| Judge:',JUDGE_MODEL,'| Qwen:',QWEN_MODEL)"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Held-out evaluation set"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"CASES=[\n('E01',\"A: Maybe move launch to Monday. B: No, keep Friday. B: I'll send QA by 3.\",['keep friday'],[('send qa','B')],[],[]),\n('E02',\"A: Export is missing IDs. B: I'll ask Finance to fix them.\",[],[('ask finance','B')],['missing ids'],[]),\n('E03',\"A: Could we use vendor B? B: Legal has not reviewed it. A: Do not choose yet.\",['do not choose'],[],['legal has not reviewed'],[]),\n('E04',\"A: Weekly dashboard might help. B: No cadence decision. B: I'll collect examples.\",[],[('collect examples','B')],[],[]),\n('E05',\"A: Import failed on invalid dates. B: I'll fix dates today. A: Keep current mapping.\",['keep current mapping'],[('fix dates','B')],['invalid dates'],[]),\n('E06',\"A: Use Sep 1 through Sep 30 for both reports. B: I'll rerun them tomorrow.\",['use sep 1 through sep 30'],[('rerun','B')],[],[]),\n('E07',\"A: We could automate email. B: Not in v1; human review is required. A: I'll document the gate.\",['human review is required'],[('document the gate','A')],[],[]),\n('E08',\"A: Duplicate customers cause bad totals. B: I'll test customer ID as the key.\",[],[('test customer id','B')],['duplicate customers'],[]),\n('E09',\"A: Should we remove notes? B: Not yet. We agreed to keep the shorter form. A: I'll measure completion time.\",['keep the shorter form'],[('measure completion time','A')],[],['remove notes']),\n('E10',\"A: SSO effort is unknown. B: Do not promise it yet. B: I'll ask Engineering. A: Do we need a separate coreference model?\",['do not promise sso'],[('ask engineering','B')],['sso effort unknown'],['coreference model'])\n]\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame([{'case':x[0],'transcript':x[1]} for x in CASES]))"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Reused retrieval and few-shot components\n\nThe RAG corpus is operational guidance, not external factual knowledge. The few-shot pool is separate from the held-out cases. This cell displays both pools and a sample dense-retrieval + cross-encoder reranking result."},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"RULES=[\n'Confirmed decisions require explicit commitment.',\n'Suggestions or maybe/could/might statements are not decisions unless later committed.',\n'Action items are future work; never invent an owner.',\n'Blockers prevent, delay, or risk progress.',\n'Follow-up questions must remain unresolved.',\n'All extracted items must be grounded in transcript evidence.'\n]\nSHOTS=[\n('Maybe delay. No, keep Friday.','decision: keep Friday'),\n('Could we use vendor B? Compare legal terms first.','no decision'),\n(\"Export is missing IDs. I'll ask Finance.\",'action item'),\n('Legal has not reviewed terms.','blocker'),\n('Should we remove notes?','follow-up question')\n]\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame({'rule':RULES}))\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(SHOTS,columns=['input','target']))\nemb=SentenceTransformer('sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\nrer=CrossEncoder('cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2')\nrv=emb.encode(RULES,normalize_embeddings=True).astype('float32'); ri=faiss.IndexFlatIP(rv.shape[1]); ri.add(rv)\nsv=emb.encode([x[0] for x in SHOTS],normalize_embeddings=True).astype('float32'); si=faiss.IndexFlatIP(sv.shape[1]); si.add(sv)\ndef ret(q,docs,idx,text=lambda x:x,k=3):\n qv=emb.encode([q],normalize_embeddings=True).astype('float32'); ds,ids=idx.search(qv,min(6,len(docs)))\n c=[(docs[int(i)],float(s)) for s,i in zip(ds[0],ids[0]) if i>=0]\n rs=rer.predict([(q,text(x[0])) for x in c]); z=[(x[0],x[1],float(r)) for x,r in zip(c,rs)]\n return sorted(z,key=lambda x:x[2],reverse=True)[:k]\ndef rules(t): return [x[0] for x in ret(t,RULES,ri,k=4)]\ndef shots(t): return [x[0] for x in ret(t,SHOTS,si,text=lambda x:x[0],k=3)]\ndemo=CASES[0][1]\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(ret(demo,RULES,ri,k=4),columns=['rule','dense','rerank']))\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame([(x[0][0],x[0][1],x[1],x[2]) for x in ret(demo,SHOTS,si,text=lambda x:x[0],k=3)],columns=['input','target','dense','rerank']))"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Structured extraction and deterministic metrics"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"PROMPT='''Return JSON only:\n{\"executive_summary\":\"string\",\"decisions\":[{\"decision\":\"string\",\"evidence\":\"string\"}],\"action_items\":[{\"description\":\"string\",\"owner\":\"string\",\"evidence\":\"string\"}],\"blockers\":[{\"blocker\":\"string\",\"evidence\":\"string\"}],\"follow_up_questions\":[{\"question\":\"string\",\"evidence\":\"string\"}]}\nOnly confirmed decisions. Do not invent owners. Blockers must delay/risk progress. Questions must remain unresolved. Include evidence.''\'\ndef valid(b): return isinstance(b,dict) and all(k in b for k in ['executive_summary','decisions','action_items','blockers','follow_up_questions'])\ndef extract(t,cfg):\n global LIVE_SYNTHESIS\n k=key(['s',GEMINI_MODEL,cfg,t])\n if k in CACHE['synthesis']: return CACHE['synthesis'][k]\n if LIVE_SYNTHESIS>=MAX_SYNTHESIS_CALLS: raise RuntimeError('synthesis cap')\n p=[PROMPT]; log={'rules':[],'examples':[]}\n if cfg in ('B','C'):\n  log['rules']=rules(t); p.append(chr(10).join(['Guidance:']+['- '+x for x in log['rules']]))\n if cfg=='C':\n  log['examples']=shots(t); p.append(chr(10).join(['Examples:']+[f'- {a} => {b}' for a,b in log['examples']]))\n p+=['Transcript:',t]\n st=time.perf_counter(); r=call(GEMINI_MODEL,[{'role':'user','content':chr(10).join(p)}]); lat=time.perf_counter()-st\n try:b=pj(r.choices[0].message.content)\n except Exception:b={}\n out={'brief':b,'valid':valid(b),'latency_s':lat,'retrieval':log}; CACHE['synthesis'][k]=out; LIVE_SYNTHESIS+=1; return out\nSTOP=set('the a an to of and or for in on by with is are be as at this that'.split())\ndef sim(a,b):\n A=set(re.findall(r'[a-z0-9]+',a.lower()))-STOP; B=set(re.findall(r'[a-z0-9]+',b.lower()))-STOP\n return len(A&B)/len(A|B) if A and B else 0\ndef f1(pred,gold):\n used=set();tp=0\n for p in pred:\n  z=[(sim(p,g),i) for i,g in enumerate(gold) if i not in used]\n  if z and max(z)[0]>=.25: tp+=1;used.add(max(z)[1])\n P=tp/len(pred) if pred else (1 if not gold else 0);R=tp/len(gold) if gold else (1 if not pred else 0)\n return 2*P*R/(P+R) if P+R else 0\ndef score(c,r):\n _,_,gd,ga,gb,gq=c;b=r['brief'] if r.get('valid') else {}\n d=[x.get('decision','') for x in b.get('decisions',[])];a=[x.get('description','') for x in b.get('action_items',[])]\n o=[x.get('owner','') for x in b.get('action_items',[])];bl=[x.get('blocker','') for x in b.get('blockers',[])];q=[x.get('question','') for x in b.get('follow_up_questions',[])]\n owner=1 if not ga else int(any(i<len(o) and o[i].lower()==go.lower() and sim(a[i],g)>=.25 for i in range(len(a)) for g,go in ga))\n return {'case':c[0],'decision_f1':f1(d,gd),'action_f1':f1(a,[x[0] for x in ga]),'owner_accuracy':owner,'blocker_f1':f1(bl,gb),'question_f1':f1(q,gq),'valid':int(r.get('valid',False)),'latency_s':r.get('latency_s',math.nan)}\nRESULTS={};rows=[]\nif os.getenv('GEMINI_API_KEY'):\n for cfg in 'ABC':\n  RESULTS[cfg]={}\n  for c in CASES:\n   try:r=extract(c[1],cfg)\n   except Exception as e: print(cfg,c[0],e);r={'brief':{},'valid':False,'latency_s':math.nan,'retrieval':{'rules':[],'examples':[]}}\n   RESULTS[cfg][c[0]]=r;s=score(c,r);s['config']=cfg;rows.append(s)\n METRICS=pd.DataFrame(rows); SUMMARY=METRICS.groupby('config').mean(numeric_only=True).round(3)\n SUMMARY['extraction_score']=SUMMARY[['decision_f1','action_f1','owner_accuracy','blocker_f1','question_f1','valid']].mean(axis=1)\n SELECTED_CONFIG=SUMMARY.extraction_score.idxmax();display(METRICS);display(SUMMARY);print('Selected:',SELECTED_CONFIG)\nelse: print('API-BLOCKED: add GEMINI_API_KEY')"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## LLM-as-judge pass"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"JUDGE_DF=pd.DataFrame();JUDGE_SUMMARY=pd.DataFrame()\ndef judge(c,b):\n global LIVE_JUDGE\n k=key(['j',JUDGE_MODEL,c[0],b])\n if k in CACHE['judge']: return CACHE['judge'][k]\n if LIVE_JUDGE>=MAX_JUDGE_CALLS: raise RuntimeError('judge cap')\n payload={'transcript':c[1],'candidate':b,'gold':c[2:]}\n prompt='Score 1-5 on correctness, grounding, operational_usefulness. Return JSON only with those keys plus reason.'\n r=call(JUDGE_MODEL,[{'role':'user','content':prompt+chr(10)+json.dumps(payload)}]);o=pj(r.choices[0].message.content)\n CACHE['judge'][k]=o;LIVE_JUDGE+=1;return o\nif RESULTS:\n jr=[]\n for c in CASES:\n  try:jr.append({'case':c[0],**judge(c,RESULTS[SELECTED_CONFIG][c[0]]['brief'])})\n  except Exception as e:print('judge',c[0],e)\n JUDGE_DF=pd.DataFrame(jr)\n if not JUDGE_DF.empty:\n  display(JUDGE_DF);JUDGE_SUMMARY=JUDGE_DF[['correctness','grounding','operational_usefulness']].mean().to_frame('average').round(3);display(JUDGE_SUMMARY)"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Required failure mode and mitigation"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"FAILURE=None;MITIGATION_BEFORE=MITIGATION_AFTER=None\nif RESULTS:\n sc={g:{c[0]:score(c,RESULTS[g][c[0]]) for c in CASES} for g in 'ABC'}; chosen=comp=None\n for c in CASES:\n  if sc['C'][c[0]]['decision_f1']<sc['B'][c[0]]['decision_f1']: chosen,comp=c[0],'dynamic few-shot';break\n if chosen is None:\n  for c in CASES:\n   if sc['B'][c[0]]['decision_f1']<sc['A'][c[0]]['decision_f1']: chosen,comp=c[0],'retrieval/reranking';break\n if chosen is None: chosen=min((c[0] for c in CASES),key=lambda x:sc[SELECTED_CONFIG][x]['decision_f1']);comp='generation'\n FAILURE={'case':chosen,'component':comp};print(FAILURE)\n for g in 'ABC':\n  print(g,json.dumps(RESULTS[g][chosen]['brief'],indent=2),RESULTS[g][chosen]['retrieval'])\nH=['maybe','could','might','consider','possibly'];K=['agreed','approved','keep','use ','do not','required']\ndef mitigate(b):\n z=json.loads(json.dumps(b));z['decisions']=[d for d in z.get('decisions',[]) if not(any(h in d.get('evidence','').lower() for h in H) and not any(k in d.get('evidence','').lower() for k in K))];return z\nif RESULTS:\n before=[];after=[]\n for c in CASES:\n  r=RESULTS[SELECTED_CONFIG][c[0]];before.append(score(c,r)['decision_f1']);r2=dict(r);r2['brief']=mitigate(r['brief']);r2['valid']=valid(r2['brief']);after.append(score(c,r2)['decision_f1'])\n MITIGATION_BEFORE=round(float(np.mean(before)),3);MITIGATION_AFTER=round(float(np.mean(after)),3);print('before',MITIGATION_BEFORE,'after',MITIGATION_AFTER)"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Gemini vs small local Qwen"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"SET=[('Maybe move launch.','context'),('Keep Friday.','decision'),(\"I'll send QA.\",'action_item'),('SSO effort unknown.','blocker'),('What is SSO effort?','follow_up_question'),('No cadence decision.','context'),('Keep mapping.','decision'),(\"I'll fix dates.\",'action_item'),('Legal has not reviewed.','blocker'),('Which agreement can Legal clear?','follow_up_question'),('We agreed to shorter form.','decision'),(\"I'll measure time.\",'action_item'),('Reports differ because dates differ.','blocker'),('Use Sep 1-Sep 30.','decision'),('Could we automate email?','context'),('Human review required.','decision'),(\"I'll test customer ID.\",'action_item'),('Is customer ID populated?','follow_up_question'),('Owner field wrong.','blocker'),('Need separate coreference model?','follow_up_question')]\ndef gclass():\n global LIVE_CLASSIFIER\n k=key(['c',GEMINI_MODEL,SET])\n if k in CACHE['classifier']:return CACHE['classifier'][k]\n lines=['Classify each span: decision, action_item, blocker, follow_up_question, context.','Return JSON only: {\"labels\":[]}.']+[f'{i+1}. {t}' for i,(t,_) in enumerate(SET)]\n st=time.perf_counter();r=call(GEMINI_MODEL,[{'role':'user','content':chr(10).join(lines)}]);lat=time.perf_counter()-st;o={'labels':pj(r.choices[0].message.content)['labels'],'latency_s':lat};CACHE['classifier'][k]=o;LIVE_CLASSIFIER+=1;return o\nGDF=pd.DataFrame();QDF=pd.DataFrame();MODEL_COMPARISON=pd.DataFrame()\nif os.getenv('GEMINI_API_KEY'):\n try:\n  g=gclass();GDF=pd.DataFrame([{'gold':gold,'pred':p,'correct':gold==p,'latency_s':g['latency_s']/20} for (_,gold),p in zip(SET,g['labels'])]);display(GDF)\n except Exception as e:print('Gemini classifier:',e)\ntry:\n import torch\n from transformers import AutoTokenizer,AutoModelForCausalLM\n tok=AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(QWEN_MODEL);qm=AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(QWEN_MODEL,torch_dtype='auto');qm.eval()\n def qc(t):\n  m=[{'role':'system','content':'Return one label only: decision, action_item, blocker, follow_up_question, context.'},{'role':'user','content':t}]\n  x=tok(tok.apply_chat_template(m,tokenize=False,add_generation_prompt=True),return_tensors='pt');st=time.perf_counter()\n  with torch.no_grad(): y=qm.generate(**x,max_new_tokens=8,do_sample=False)\n  p=tok.decode(y[0][x['input_ids'].shape[1]:],skip_special_tokens=True).strip().lower();return re.sub(r'[^a-z_]','',p),time.perf_counter()-st\n QDF=pd.DataFrame([{'gold':g,'pred':p,'correct':g==p,'latency_s':l} for t,g in SET for p,l in [qc(t)]]);display(QDF)\nexcept Exception as e:print('Qwen:',e)\nrows=[]\nif not GDF.empty:rows.append({'model':'Gemini Flash','accuracy':GDF.correct.mean(),'mean_latency_s':GDF.latency_s.mean()})\nif not QDF.empty:rows.append({'model':QWEN_MODEL,'accuracy':QDF.correct.mean(),'mean_latency_s':QDF.latency_s.mean()})\nMODEL_COMPARISON=pd.DataFrame(rows)\nif not MODEL_COMPARISON.empty:display(MODEL_COMPARISON.round(3))"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Research note"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"def note():\n if not RESULTS or JUDGE_DF.empty or FAILURE is None:return None\n jt='\\n'.join(f\"- **{i}:** {float(r['average']):.3f}\" for i,r in JUDGE_SUMMARY.iterrows())\n qt='Qwen comparison incomplete.'\n if len(MODEL_COMPARISON)>=2:\n  g=MODEL_COMPARISON.iloc[0];q=MODEL_COMPARISON.iloc[1];qt=f\"Qwen accuracy {q.accuracy:.3f} vs Gemini {g.accuracy:.3f}; latency {q.mean_latency_s:.3f}s vs {g.mean_latency_s:.3f}s.\"\n s=f'''# Research Note — Meeting-to-Action Assistant\n\n## Measured results\n\n{SUMMARY.to_markdown()}\n\n### LLM-as-judge\nSelected: **{SELECTED_CONFIG}**\n\n{jt}\n\n### Failure\nCase **{FAILURE['case']}**, component **{FAILURE['component']}**.\n\n### Mitigation\nDecision F1 before **{MITIGATION_BEFORE}**, after **{MITIGATION_AFTER}**.\n\n### Gemini vs local Qwen\n{qt}\n\n### Final architecture decision\nKeep the simplest measured configuration with the strongest held-out score. Use Gemini for full meeting interpretation/synthesis; keep retrieval, reranking, validation, metrics, and mitigation local/deterministic. Use Qwen only if the measured narrow-classification result justifies it.\n'''\n display(Markdown(s));return s\nRESEARCH_NOTE=note()"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":"## Submission guard"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":"p=[]\nif not RESULTS:p.append('A/B/C evaluation')\nif JUDGE_DF.empty or len(JUDGE_DF)!=10:p.append('10-case judge')\nif FAILURE is None:p.append('failure trace')\nif MODEL_COMPARISON.empty or len(MODEL_COMPARISON)<2:p.append('Gemini/Qwen comparison')\nif RESEARCH_NOTE is None:p.append('research note')\nprint('READY FOR SUBMISSION' if not p else 'NOT READY FOR SUBMISSION: '+', '.join(p))\nprint('CACHE_EXPORT =',json.dumps(CACHE,separators=(',',':')))\nprint('HTML: jupyter nbconvert --to html week8_meeting_to_action_capstone.ipynb')"}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.11"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}